Ashrumite is the hometown of the Gnome race. The city is reached by a long rough road leading in from the east. Much of the city itself is underground, in a vast
network of mines and tunnels. Strong guards protect the
main road and the gates from evil invasion forces.
     Hint The Inn is also a Healing Room
All directions are from the INN:
*1w 1d                      :    The Bartender
*1w 1d 2n 1d 2n 2w 2n 1d 2s   :  The Banker
*1w 1d 2n 1d 2n 8w   :           The W Gates
*1w 1d 2n 1d 2n 9e   :           The E Gates
*1w 1d 2n 1d 1e  :                     Shop
*1w 1d 2n 1d 1w  :                     Shop
*1w 1d 2n 1d 1s 1e  :                  Shop
==See also==
quest, bartender, gnome, hometowns Category : Directions

#0

Ask
Ask - Last Edited: 2008-03-26 18:02:34 by Blaize
================================================
* say <text>
* tell <character> <text>
* whisper <character> <text>
* ask <character> <text>
* project <text>
In order to communicate with other players, you must begin your sentences
with one of the above commands.  Use "say" if you wish everyone in the room
to hear you (unless they are asleep - characters who are asleep are
incommunicado, except to the Staff). "Tell," "whisper" and "ask" are used
to keep your conversations private and must be accompanied by the name of
the player with whom you wish to converse.  "Whisper" and "ask" can only
be used if the player you want to converse with is the same room.  "Tell"
is for global communication.  You can "tell" anyone who is awake, is not
in a dark room or invis and has tell on, no matter where they are in the
mud.
Please do not ask the Staff to tell a person that you can't reply to them.
You will have to wait until they are visible and do it yourself.
Note:  "tell" is a user command, and is only available to make the game
more playable.
Syntax:  toggle tell
Toggling "tell" will effectively allow you to toggle off this line of
communication.  However, it will not prevent a staff member from speaking
to you.
==See also==
* Commands
* Listen
* Tell
* Toggle
* Whisper

#0

Ass
Ass - Last Edited: 2008-03-26 18:05:50 by Blaize
================================================
Ass, is short for being "on one's ass."  While on one's ass, melee
damage received is greatly increased (about x2 damage).
One can voluntarily put himself on his ass.  Simply recline.
Additionally, one can knock another to his ass via a successful
bodyslam and sometimes with a successful trip.
When a mercenary fails a tackle, they often end up assed for a long
time. Sometimes a failed bash results in being assed, likewise.
Should one flee while in a reclined position, he will simply
scramble to his feet rather than failing entirely like most other
actions.
==See also==
* Bodylam
* Flee
* Reclined
* Sit
* Trip

