#0

Bash
Bash - Last Edited: 2013-04-26 15:44:48 by targ
===============================================
Syntax:         bash <victim>
To bash someone is to attempt to knock that person over. If you succeed,
you will inflict minor damage and cause the victim to fall down. Both you
and the victim will then be unable to respond to any commands for a short
duration. If you fail to bash successfully, you will lose your balance and
fall. It is impossible to bash someone who is sitting/resting already. It is
much easier to bash someone if you are using a shield. Some creatures
may be unbashable due to size or other considerations.
A successful bash depends upon the dexterity of the basher and the agility
of the target. Characters with higher dexterity will be successful more often.
NOTE: Bash will not work in places where there is no footing.
==See also==
warrior, paladin, bodyslam, kneel, shieldless bash

