Chuckle
Chuckle - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
=====================================================
Chuckle is a social command, or an Emote. Typing this command will allow you to Chuckle, using preprogrammed commands. The benefits of using these commands will allow you in one word to sum up a long phrase, and social commands are sometimes used as triggers. More often they are a nice simple command to express yourself. The command list is as follows.
Chuckle = You chuckle politely.
Chuckle me/self = You chuckle to yourself.
Chuckle (target name) = You chuckle politely at(target names)
==See also==
Emote, Social Actions, commands

#0

Circle
Circle - Last Edited: 2009-06-01 18:53:22 by Blaize
===================================================
Syntax:         circle <victim>
* Aggressive:     Yes
Circling is an attempt to outflank an opponent in battle and to attack from
unexpected positions.  When successful, the victim will find it much more
difficult to dodge and parry the rogue's vicious attack and will take
considerably more damage.  Circle cannot be initiated when the rogue is
tanking.
"Circle" also refers to spheres of knowledge of spell casting classes, with
higher circles denoting more powerful groups of spells. Spell casters (all
Mage and Priest sub-classes) and "semi-casters" (Rangers, Paladins, and
Anti-Paladins) gain in circle at levels 1, 6, 11, 16, 21, 26, 31, 36, 41,
46, 51, and 56.
You cannot circle someone in a single file room.
==See Also==
*Backstab
*Flank
*Spell circle
*Tank

