Comb
Comb - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
==================================================
Comb is a social command, or an Emote. Typing this command will allow you to Comb your hair, using preprogrammed commands. The benefits of using these commands will allow you in one word to sum up a long phrase, and social commands are sometimes used as triggers. More often they are a nice simple command to express yourself. The command list is as follows.
Comb = You comb your hair - perfect.
Comb me/self = You pull your hair, but it will not be combed.
Comb (target name) = You patiently untangle (Target Name)'s hair - what a mess!
==See also==
Emote, Social Actions, commands

#0

Combat mind
Combat mind - Last Edited: 2009-06-13 03:01:57 by Blaize
========================================================
Updated: 12Jun09
* Area of effect: <self>
* Aggressive:     No
* Cumulative:     N/A
* Duration:       Dependent on caster
* Type of spell:  Enchantment
This spell prepares your mind and body for the rigors of close combat. The target's
hit and damage roll increases. Higher level casters see greater benefits. This spell
is far more effective on a psionicist than any other class. When combat mind affects
a psionicist, he or she is able gain additional attacks, hit roll, damage roll, and
parry incoming blows if wielding a weapon.
== See also ==
* Psionicist

#0

Combination attack
Combination attack - Last Edited: 2017-01-12 03:46:26 by lohrr
==============================================================
Syntax: Combination
While a monk is engaged with another creature, one of the monk's most damaging abilities is its
combination attack.  It takes a couple rounds to setup, but during this time the monk may (and
should) use another ability such as his/her dragon punch or springleap (just don't fall down
before the combination attack would go off).  As the monk increases in level, the combination
attack will include more attacks and eventually it may even stun the target.
==See also==
Monk, Skills, Dragon Punch, Springleap, Stun

