#0

Corpse
Corpse - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
====================================================
A corpse is a cadaver left behind after a mob or person has been killed.  A corpse will decay after a small amount of time, and the spell "preserve" is used to delay such action.  Corpses often contain coins and gear, and sometimes can contain hidden items found by "search corpse".  A PC's corpse can be resurrected by the cleric spell "resurrection" allowing the player to return to the spot of the corpse, and retain some of the exp lost upon death.  Corpses are the main tool that necromancers utilize upon raising inanimate beings.
Also see:  Help search, Help resurrection, Help necromancer, Help preserve

#0

Corpseform
Corpseform - Last Edited: 2007-09-27 17:10:52 by kyse
=====================================================
* Area of effect: <corpse>
* Aggressive:     No
* Cumulative:     No
* Duration:       Dependent on proficiency of caster
* Type of spell:  Enchantment
With a corpse at their feet, Corpseform will transform the caster into the
race of that corpse. This will cause them to be viewed as that race by their foes
and comrades alike. Rumor has it that there is also a small chance during the
process that the racial powers/weaknesses are transferred to the caster as well.
Due to the heavy concentration required while using this spell the caster may not
control undead.
	See also:Elemental Aura, Vampiric Trance

