Cr
Cr - Last Edited: 2009-04-17 23:14:39 by Blaize
===============================================
A cr is a acronym for "corpse retrieval".
After the death of your character, you will return to the game without your
personal items. To get your items back, you have to travel to the location
where you died and retrieve your corpse. Your items will be on your corpse,
unless they have been looted by someone else.
A cr can be simple, or it can be very time-consuming and complicated. It is
always a wise move to leave a ''sitter'' if you are doing a difficult zone.
Please see help rules.
==See also==
* Death
* Loot
* Massrip
* Sitter

#0

Craft
Craft - Last Edited: 2015-08-18 04:51:06 by ashyel
==================================================
Craft is one of the tradeskills available to players.
Craft allows characters to create equipment for following slots:
about, waist, earring, neck, wrist, finger, eyes, quiver, tail, nose, horn, face.
Once learned, a player can invoke the forge command for a list of options.
Crafting uses components obtained through the salvage skill to allow players
to create the items themselves!
craft - with no arguments will bring up your list of known recipes and the help
menu:
(example:)
craft Syntax:
(craft info - list required materials to forge the item.)
(craft stat - display properties of the item.)
(craft make - create the item.)
You know the following recipes:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recipe Number Item
135212 a wickedly barbed two-handed greatsword
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
91058 a massive blood-stained holy avenger
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Typing 'craft info 91058' would display the items needed to create this particular
item.
Typing 'craft stat 91058' would display the attributes tied to this item.
Typing 'craft make 91058' would attempt to create the item if you had the necessary
salvaged materials on your being.
Please note: Crafting is only possible on items with an ivalue of less than 100.
==See also==
tradeskills, forge, material_list, salvage

#0

Cramped
Cramped - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
=====================================================
A cramped room is a very tiny pathway with only 2 exits.
When entering a cramped room, all players and mobs are forced into a single file line, and may only cast spells and engage those who are next to them.  Additionally, only those near the exits may leave the room normally.  All others will bump into those who are standing in the room.
To get through a cramped room, one should recline.  Moving while in such position results in a squirming action, which while is not always effective, can get through the cramped room.  It is much too difficult to squirm past those who are fighting in a cramped room.
Area spells and transportation spells are also unusable in cramped rooms.
While mounted, one cannot fit through these tiny pathways.
==See Also==
recline

