#0

Emote
Emote - Last Edited: 2007-04-19 19:17:11 by Unknown
===================================================
Syntax:  emote <message_text>
         : <message_text>
The "emote" command allows you to creatively pretend that your
character is doing something that the available socials do not
currently allow.  For example, if Fizzwig wished everyone to think he
is a really nice guy, he might type:
        emote hands you 10000 pcoins.
                -or-
        : hands you 10000 pcoins.
This would be viewed as everyone in the room as:
        Fizzwig hands you 10000 pcoins.
Of course, Fizzwig has not really given anyone the coins, he just
wants everyone to think he has.
A quicker, equivalent command is ":"
Note:  "emote" is a social action that is used for *fun*.  Please do not
take these actions seriously.
==See also==
Social Actions

#0

Enchant
Enchant - Last Edited: 2008-11-24 15:16:20 by Blaize
====================================================
This skill will imbue a piece of equipment of your choosing with any spell
up to a certain power that is currently affecting the casting player.
There are some restrictions in the type of spells that may be enchanted.
- Artifacts cannot be enchanted.
- Offensive spells or any spells that are of the "self only" cast type cannot
be enchanted into the item.
- Only one enchant affect can be held on a piece of equipment at any one time
and the effect will wear off in the appropriate time span.
Enchanting an item can be an expensive exercise and you will need to carry
the necessary funds to use this skill. An enchanted item will display a flag
indicating that status if successful, however, beware that unsuccessful
enchant attempts may permanently damage the item in the process.
Example Syntax: enchant cloak 'vitality'
The knowledge of this ability is imparted by a Dwarven Smith within a Tribal
Oasis.
NOTE: Choosing to learn this epic skill will prevent the player from pursuing
any knowledge in the Spellbind epic skill.
==See also==
* Epic Skills
* Spellbind
* Spells

#0

Enchant Weapon
Enchant Weapon - Last Edited: 2007-04-20 14:02:09 by Unknown
============================================================
* Area of effect: <weapon>
* Aggressive:     N0
* Cumulative:     No
* Duration:       Permanent
* Type of spell:  Enchantment
"Enchant Weapon" will enchant non-magical (non-modifying) weapons only.
Non-modifying weapons are those that do not alter any ability. The only way
 to be certain if a weapon is suitable for enchantment is to fully identify
it.
The level of enchantment given the weapon is random, depending upon
conditions of the weather, magical energies, skill of the conjurer, and the
blessings of the gods.
	See also:identify ,weather

