Feeding
Feeding - Last Edited: 2014-07-31 19:17:39 by ashyel
====================================================
On Duris, artifacts, uniques, and iouns are in need of "feeding", which can be done through gaining epics or the spilling of blood through PvP.
.
Artifacts come with an initial timer which can be supplemented by epic zoning or fragging enemies.  If you fail to feed, your artifact will be removed and placed back into the game where it loads when the timer counts down.
See also:  artifact ,unique ,ioun

#0

Feign death
Feign death - Last Edited: 2008-01-29 13:02:41 by torgal
========================================================
Syntax:         feign death
"Feign Death" is a rather clever way of fooling all those nearby into
believing that you have died. In actuality, you are alive and in hiding.
You then have a good chance of escaping in one piece since only the most
astute of enemies can determine that you are still alive.

#0

Ferries
Ferries - Last Edited: 2015-08-05 21:05:20 by ashyel
====================================================
Currently in the world of Duris there are three large ocean-going vessels that traverse the seas, ferrying passengers to different locations.  Players who cannot afford or do not wish to purchase their own ships can use these ferries to travel.
Tickets for these vessels can be purchased from Gnomish contraptions positioned near each docking point.  Players may ride a ferry as far as they choose, but must buy a new ticket once they've disembarked.
==The WaveDancer==
Departs from the ports of Quietus Quay, Myrabolus, and the Jade Empire beach at a cost of 10 platinum per ticket.
==The SeaStalker==
Travels between Storm Port, the NW beach of Khomeni Khan and the City of Torrhan at a cost of 30 platinum per ticket.
==The Seaspray==
Travels between Menden, Fort Boyard, and StormPort at a cost of 10 platinum per ticket.
==The Old Ferry==
Travels between Menden and Fenaline at a cost of 5 platinum per ticket.
==See also==
ships, moonwell, map

