Forge
Forge - Last Edited: 2013-05-07 15:25:44 by targ
================================================
Forge is one of the tradeskills available to players.
Forge allows characters to create equipment for the following slots:
head, body, arms, feet, shield, weapons, legs, hands.
Once learned, a player can invoke the forge command for a list of options:
forge - with no arguments will bring up your list of known recipes and the help
menu:
(example:)
Forge Syntax:
(forge info <number> - list required materials to forge the item.)
(forge stat <number> - display properties of the item.)
(forge make <number> - create the item.)
You know the following recipes:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Recipe Number                         Item
   135212                a wickedly barbed two-handed greatsword
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   91058                 a massive blood-stained holy avenger
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Typing 'forge info 91058' would display the items needed to create this particular
item.
Typing 'forge stat 91058' would display the attributes tied to this item.
Typing 'forge make 91058' would attempt to create the item if you had the necessary
salvaged materials on your being.
==See also==
tradeskills, craft, salvage, material_list

#0

Forget
Forget - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
====================================================
Forget is a command used to remove a spell from your current list of spells.
Forget alone will clear your list of spells to be memorized or prayed; whereas,
"forget all" will empty your mind of all spells. When you "forget <spell name>"
it will remove the spell from your list to be memorized or prayed first, then,
if no more exist in that list then they will be removed from spells you have
already committed to memory.
==See also==
pray, memorize, spells, Spell Circle, Spell Slot, cast

