Gate to ardgral
Gate to ardgral - Last Edited: 2008-10-08 02:36:35 by Jexni
===========================================================
* Area of effect: <room>
* Aggressive: No
* Cumulative: No
* Duration: Dependent on proficiency of caster
* Type of spell: Transportation
Gate to Ard'gral opens up a gate to Ard'gral the Quasi-Elemental plane of dreams, where rifts open up to all parts of the world and other planes. Here's how Plane of Ard'gral works: there are gateways that lead to random spots on surface, and they're random when you enter them. So if person A enters the gateway, and person B immediately enters the same gateway, you could wind up on different parts of map. Now there are rifts and pools (much like on Ethereal Plane) to other planes (Astral Plane|Astral, Ethereal Plane|Ethereal, Elemental Plane of Earth|Earth, Elemental Plane of Water|Water, Elemental Plane of Fire|Fire, Elemental Plane of Air|Air). There are also a couple of rifts to other "fixed" zones like Bloodstone, Vella's Bordello, and The Killing Fields. All the greatest places that folks on Duris dream about. It is up to you to figure out what type of rift goes where. Oh, and all rifts and gateways are one-way.
==See also==
Illusionist, gateway, spells

#0

Gaze
Gaze - Last Edited: 2009-04-28 23:34:59 by Blaize
=================================================
The gaping empty sockets of the Dreadlord and Avenger may be sightless, but
its gaze contains something much more searching, disturbing and terrifying
than most mortals may bear. To have the gaze of a Dreadlord or Avenger upon
you is to know true fear. Too petrified to move, your world ceasing and
stopping as you struggle to free and turn away. The ability to gaze is
dependent on the attribute power of the attacker. It is not crucial but
will help subdue the victim.
The terrifying gaze has been rumored to cause spellcasters to stop casting!
==See also==
* Avenger
* Dreadlord

