God
God - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
=================================================
ALL Staff members, regardless of level, should be shown respect. Do NOT ask for interference or game information from a Staff member. The Staff abides by the non-interference policy and can NOT assist you in retrieving corpses, give directions to places, teleport you, communicate messages to invisible players, give information on equipment, areas or mobs, preserve corpses, etc...  If you hear of someone that has gotten such aid in this manner, do NOT complain to the Staff. The Staff do NOT interfere UNLESS THERE IS A PROVEN BUG OR SPECIAL CIRCUMSTANCES HAVE ARISEN. Any such cumstances must have the approval of a FORGER. Do NOT ask Staff members for clarification on any "help" or "favoritism" another player has received, it is, in all honesty, none of your business.  We do NOT show favoritism, and will resent anyone who implies this.  If you feel someone has gotten favoritism from a Staff member, most likely you do NOT know the full story and you will just have to trust our judgement on this.
==See also==
rules, petition

#0

God call
God call - Last Edited: 2007-09-21 23:07:04 by zion
===================================================
Syntax:         innate god call
The Cleric has the ability to call upon their God to come to their aid. Before specialization, this ability will have one of three effects. After specialization, it will have only one effect.
Zealot:
The zealot will call upon the gods to strengthen him in the ways of combat. For the duration the cleric will gain melee attacks and also receive a boost to his hitroll and damroll.
Holyman:
The blessing of the gods will blanket the room with peace causing all players and npc characters to disengage from combat. It will also clear all
the mobs tracking the cleric.
Healer:
Using the god call as a healer will result in a group buff, that will increase
the healing amount of all healing spells while the buff is active.
==See also==
* Speclist

