Godpoofin
Godpoofin - Last Edited: 2026-10-18
=======================================================
"poofin <text>" sets your arrival message for "goto". "poofout <text>"
sets your departure message. Each message can contain up to 512 characters,
including color codes. An overlong message leaves your current setting intact.

Use %n to put your name anywhere in the message. Without %n, your name is
added at the beginning. Example: poofin A swirl of mist reveals %n.

Type "poofin ?" or "poofout ?" to preview the message. Type "poofin" or
"poofout" without arguments to restore the default. Messages are shown only
to people who can see you. Teleport and transfer use their own messages.

See also: god goto, POOFIN, POOFOUT

#0

Godptell
Godptell - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
======================================================
Syntax:  ptell <player> <text>
This is exactly like tell, except that <text> is broadcast to all gods
with petition toggled on, to let them know that you responded to a
particular petition.

When enabled, the optional staff-only Discord petition feed also receives one
copy of an accepted ptell, labeled with the actual sender and target character
names, including when hidden, invisible, or using mortal fog. Discord posts
cannot become game replies. Native recipients, visibility, toggles, and logs
are unchanged; delivery is best effort.

Example:
        Oinkoink petitions "Why is the sky blue?"
You reply:
        ptell oinkoink shut the hell up before I term you!
Which displays to the gods as:
        Petition: <your_name> responds to Oinkoink"s petition with
        "shut the hell up before I term you!"
==========================================================================
#
"GOD, PURGE"

