Grid
Grid - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
==================================================
A system of reference lines that intersect at right angles to form uniformly sized squares.  Often but not always the squares can be 3 dimensional in shape.  For example a grid might be a 3 X 3 square, in which that grid would be 3 spaces in all directions including up and down.  Many of the planes feature grids that will loop on there grids.  When laying out a zone forming a grid often is helpful in designing the first area of a zone.
==See also==
areamaking, zonegod

