#0

Holy Sacrifice
Holy Sacrifice - Last Edited: 2026-10-18
=====================================
* Paladin circle: 10th (Cavalier, Crusader)
* Area of effect: <caster> & <group>
* Aggressive:     No
* Cumulative:     No
* Duration:       15 ticks, plus 1 for every 10 points of Devotion
* Type of spell:  Healing
As the Paladin sheds blood in combat, their suffering mends the wounds of
their comrades. While it lasts, each blow the Paladin takes heals every
groupmate in the same room by up to 30% of the damage dealt, but never past
that groupmate's maximum hit points.

The healing a single blow can share is limited. In total, one blow heals the
group by no more than 90% of its damage, and never more than 60% of the
Paladin's own maximum hit points. Across a whole combat round the group can
receive at most 120% of the Paladin's maximum hit points. In a small group
each groupmate usually receives the full 30% before healing modifiers; in a
large group the healing is divided among those who need it. A blow from a
player, including their pet or borrowed form, halves these limits for the
rest of the combat round, even if monsters also attack. Healing already
received counts toward that smaller allowance; no hit points are taken back.
This reduction can also reduce healing in a small group.

Groupmates who are plagued, or who carry a Holy Sacrifice of their own,
receive nothing. The sacrifice gives nothing while the Paladin is plagued,
under Blood Mantle or under Flamestrike, or when the blow comes from someone
in Battle Ecstasy.

Above 50th level, a Cavalier's summoned mount also carries this blessing.

Usage: cast 'holy sacrifice'
	See also: group, tank, Blood Tithe, Battle Ecstasy

