#0

Immolure
Immolure - Last Edited: 2008-09-18 15:20:43 by Blaize
=====================================================
To immolure or doomlure is to cause a mob to chase after you
by way of wave-type spells. This tactic is used often when mobs are grouped
together making it foolish and impractical to rush in.
A tank or pet is sent forward first, then the lurer enters, casts, and runs.
A few words of warning, this tactic does not always work the first time.
Problems arise then the tank does not flee soon enough, the pet lasts past
the end of the spell, or the mob shrugged the spell. It is also noteworthy
that mobs able to range their magic have been known to require the lurer
to run farther or turn corners in order to lure properly.
==See also==
* Acidimmolate
* Bleed
* Creeping Doom
* Doomlure
* Dread Wave
* Immolate
* Magma Burst

#0

Immortals
Immortals - Last Edited: 2009-11-24 22:04:46 by Blaize
======================================================
Immortals/Gods are people who have obtained level 57 or above. They should be
respected for donating their time and energy into making the game a better
place to play.  Immortals will adhere to these rules to the best of their
ability(situations not withstanding).
1. Immortals cannot give out information such as: statistics of a player,
   statistics of items or other private information.
2. Immortals cannot give away objects or equipment, unless mitigating circumstances
   (such as a quest) come into play and are discussed with other immortals.
3. Staff members may not actively play player characters, and active
   players may not serve as Staff. This applies across all characters and
   accounts. See &+Yhelp rules&n for the full policy.
Nobody likes rules, but we need them to keep the game fun and interesting.
Most immortals can be reached at immortalname@durismud.com.
==See also==
* Credits
* Petition
* Rules
* Wizlist

