Light
Light - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
===================================================
A light can be a torch, a lantern or a lit item.  Items can be permanently lit by the local Illusionist, or Cleric.  An item can only be lit if it is non-magical.  One can identify magical items with the 'detect magic' spell.  The disadvantage of torches and lanters is that they must be held in one hand, and they expire after an amount of time.
==See also==
cleric, illusionist, Continual Light

#0

Lightbringer
Lightbringer - Last Edited: 2026-10-18
============================================================
Lightbringer is a Avenger specialization. Selection requires level 30, an eligible race, an appropriate teacher, no existing specialization or secondary class, and an expired respecialization timer.
==Allowed races==
None. This path has no ordinary race permission row.
These permissions apply to an existing character; they do not enable a forbidden creation race/class combination. Server event settings can relax the race filter.
==Skill changes==
None beyond the base-class registrations.
==Spell changes==
None beyond the base-class registrations.
==Innate additions==
None beyond the base-class registrations.
Requirements are registration values, not automatic learning or preparation. Base-class grants remain subject to the listed specialization changes, and abilities retain their own use conditions.
==See also==
* Avenger
* Avenger Skills
* Specialization
* Unspecialization

