Look
Look - Last Edited: 2007-04-19 19:17:13 by Unknown
==================================================
"Look" is used for studying your surroundings and is more often used in its
short form variation of "l."
Eg : look
     l
     look dragon
     look at board
     look board
     l at board
     look in bag
     l in bag
     l in 2.bag (if you have more than one bag)
     l south
     l candle (if there"s an extra description of a candle in a room)
Note that if you type "look at <container>" you will not see its contents.
To see what"s inside a container (e.g., a corpse), use the syntax "look IN
<object>." For this type of inspection, it"s best to use the command
"examine."
"Look" is also used when utilizing one of Duris"s many ships, although with
different syntax.
	See also:examine ,glance ,read ,ships

#0

Loot
Loot - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
==================================================
Looting refers to getting equipment out of a corpse. In zones the leader will loot or designate someone else to loot. In raids you cannot loot if you are backranked. Also, looting player corpses (even your own) will lag you for a short time.
Ninja looting refers to the practice of quickly snatching items off a corpse for yourself when grouped.
Hoarding is another form of selfish looting. Hoarders will loot from raids and then not split with the group.
Syntax: get all corpse / get <item> corpse
==See also==
lag, get

