Massrip
Massrip - Last Edited: 2007-04-19 19:17:13 by Unknown
=====================================================
Massrip stands for "Mass R.I.P.", and come in all shapes and sizes, and generally depicts a situation where your group suddenly got bored with life while deep in a zone somewhere. This is why leaving a ''sitter'' is a good idea!
Massrips are generally followed by a long and arduous ''cr'', and is sometimes accompanied by an untimely scouting by the opposite racewar. Massrips can get very ugly.
Some of the more common reasons for a massrip include players going afk without informing the rest of the group, the group leader charging a room full of high-level angry mobs, and of course, bad luck.
Note: Make sure to give the individual who caused your massrip a hearty round of applause. The more difficult the cr, the more flagrant your approval of the situation should be!
==See also==
cr, sitter, afk, congratulate, mob

