Memorize
Memorize - Last Edited: 2022-10-08 21:57:50 by ashyel
=====================================================
Syntax:  <memorize|pray> (while resting)
Syntax:  <memorize|pray> 'spellname' (while resting)
Syntax:  forget 'spellname'
"Memorize" and "Pray" lets you put a spell in your active repertoire. To
successfully memorize or pray for a spell, you must be holding, wearing or have in
your inventory a spellbook which contains the scribed spell to
successfully memorize it.
Memorizing or praying without specifying a spellname allows you to
resume your studies/prayers and lists the time remaining to complete
each spell.
"Forget" lets you purge a spell from your active repertoire.
	See also:spellslot ,cast ,practice ,meditate

#0

Memory
Memory - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
====================================================
Memory refers to the mobs ability to remember a person who has attacked them.  Almost all mobs in Duris have memory, and about half of them will "track" the player through the zone and attack them.  Mobs will definately not track once in the deep big nasty condition, or pretty hurt condition.  To escape a tracking mob, a person may wish to leave the zone (travel to the map), to remain behind locked exists (doors), or remain invisible (assuming the mob has no detections).  Conversely if a mob is tracking you on the map you may wish to hide in a zone.  Certain caster mobs may also track the player by using "dimension door" to pop right into the room of the player.
==See also==
mob, tracking, Dimension Door

