Multiclass
Multiclass - Last Edited: 2026-10-18
============================================================
Human and Orc PCs can add an allowed secondary class. The checked-in
requirements are level 50 and a minimum epic balance of 0; server properties
may change those requirements. Type multiclass to see personal choices, then
multiclass <class> at an appropriate multiclass room. Ordered class pairs and
the race/class matrix both restrict the choice.
Multiclassing resets level and XP to 1, clears specialization and ordinary
learned skills, forgets prepared spells, refunds epic skills, clears XP
trophies and prestige, and puts a guilded character on parole. Played time is
preserved.
Primary-only skills retain their requirement and cap. Secondary-only ordinary
skills require five extra levels and use 95% of the secondary cap under the
checked-in properties; primary caps use 100%. Shared skills choose the lower
adjusted requirement and higher adjusted cap. Secondary-only spells cost one
extra circle; a primary spell keeps its own circle. A spell must fit within
the currently accessible circles.
Preparation and casting depend on primary class and race. The usual multiclass
preparation factor is 1.75. Epic rewards available only through the secondary
class apply additional factors of 2 to epic-point cost and 3 to coin cost.
Equipment restrictions still apply, including checks that use only the primary
class.
At the assigned unmulti altar, pray altar requires 100 epic points and removes
the secondary class, clears specialization, forgets prepared spells, and
updates skills. It does not restore the level, XP, or skills held before
multiclassing.
==Candidate pairs before race filtering==
* Warrior: Mercenary, Cleric
* Ranger: Warrior, Druid, Rogue, Psionicist
* Paladin: Warrior
* Anti-Paladin: Warrior
* Cleric: Druid, Bard, Warrior, Shaman
* Shaman: Conjurer, Druid, Cleric, Blighter
* Sorcerer: Conjurer
* Conjurer: Sorcerer, Shaman, Bard
* Rogue: Bard, Mercenary
* Mercenary: Rogue, Warrior
* Bard: Sorcerer, Rogue, Illusionist, Conjurer
* Reaver: Sorcerer, Rogue, Psionicist
* Ethermancer: Sorcerer, Shaman
* Summoner: Sorcerer, Shaman
==See also==
Classes, Specialization, Spell circle

