Petition
Petition - Last Edited: 2007-04-19 19:17:14 by Unknown
======================================================
Syntax:         petition <text>
The "Petition" command allows you to send a message to all of the Gods
currently on the MUD (if there are any).  Certain guidelines should be
followed when petitioning:
* Do not inquire if gods are online. Describe your problem in details
so they can come back to it later when they have time.
When the optional Discord petition feed is enabled, accepted petitions and
staff ptell replies may also appear in a staff-only Discord channel, even when
no gods are online. The feed always identifies the petitioner and both reply
participants by their character names, including when hidden or invisible.
Discord posts cannot reply into the game. Native petition recipients, toggles,
and logs remain unchanged; the feed is best effort.
==See also==
gods, togglepetition, website, forums, bug, idea, typo, tell

#0

Pets
Pets - Last Edited: 2016-04-03 19:07:37 by lohrr
================================================
"Pets" are creatures who will permanently follow you and your orders unless
you attack them or rent them off. You can aquire them in several different
ways depending on what type of character you are. Some classes have the
ability to "summon" pets. Others have the ability to "charm" a mob to make
it a pet via an innate ability or a spell. One type of character can raise
the dead to create pets. Finally, some classes are forced to purchase pets
in pet shops located throughout the world.
NOTE:     Your pet follow orders from you until you attack it, you rent or
          it dies.
See also:
follow, order, dismiss

#0
Phantom
Phantom - Last Edited: 2026-08-25 12:00:00 by duris
===================================================
Phantoms are ethereal, incorporeal undead spirits created when sentient souls are
bound into planar servitude through dark necromancy. Wandering the ruined catacombs
and desolate chambers of Ixarkon, phantoms appear as translucent, ghostly figures
surrounded by an otherworldly, luminescent aura. They drift silently above the ground,
unimpeded by physical barriers or terrain.

Phantoms exist simultaneously in the Prime Material and Astral planes. In battle, they
can manifest Phantasmal Form to phase through lethal physical strikes, and their mastery
over planar shifts allows them to evade enemy ambushes effortlessly.

==Strengths==
Phantoms possess innate magic resistance, natural flight, and planar shifting to Prime
and Astral realms. Their Phantasmal Form ability provides supreme physical evasion in
combat, and they possess keen ultravision.

==Weakness==
Phantoms are severely vulnerable to fire damage and holy energy. Their incorporeal nature
limits physical carrying capacity and raw strength.

==See also==
* Innate
* Races
* Dreadlord
* Ultravision
* Ixarkon
==Class list==
* Psionicist  :
* Conjurer    :
* Reaver      :
* Summoner    :
==Racial Statistics==
Strength    : 90
Agility     : 130
Dexterity   : 140
Constitution: 97
Power       : 125
Intelligence: 100
Wisdom      : 100
Charisma    : 100
Luck        : 100
Karma       : 100
==Racial Traits==
Combat Pulse : average
Spell Pulse  : very good
==Innate abilities==
*ultravision
 shift_astral
 shift_prime
*fly (obtained at level 21)
 phantasmal form (obtained at level 20)
*vulnerable to fire
*magic resistance
'*' Designates passive ability.

