#0

Random Equipment
Random Equipment - Last Edited: 2016-09-25 20:11:47 by lohrr
============================================================
The chaotic nature of Duris manifests itself in the spontaneous creation
of creatures, areas and equipment in places not generally found.
Random Equipment
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
These items are forged by the swirl of powers inherent upon that moment of
death, and can occasionally be found on the corpses of defeated creatures.
Random Mobs
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tossed through the ether from latent world magics gone awry, creatures far
from home can be found wandering lost on the lands. Beware approaching
these bewildered souls, as fear may drive them past all reasoning and
sanity into beings of unrivaled aggression and power.
Random Zones
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Powerful shifts and changes within the earth's crust toss up areas from the
depths. Still half buried, these require a shovel and some hard digging
before they can be accessed and explored to find what treasures and beasts
may lurk hidden and lie within. These places are rare and difficult to find.
==See also==
Zone, Mob, Equipment, Dig, Named Equipment, Random Equipment Drops

#0

Random zones
Random zones - Last Edited: 2008-04-11 14:09:39 by Blaize
=========================================================
Random zones can be found throughout the realms of Duris.
To locate a random zone, look for tombstones or slabs which
are the entrances to the random zone.  An adventurer will
need a shovel to open the random zone.  Random zones can
be extremely difficult or able to done by a low level group.
NOTE:  These zones can be extremely difficult.  Make sure you
read the sign at the entrance to see how difficult it will
be.
==See also==
* Zones

#0

Range
Range - Last Edited: 2010-02-07 01:25:20 by zion
================================================
The term range or Lure is broadly used, but it is more specifically used to describe the
action of "pulling" or "luring" a desired monster into the room, that is a room or many away.
Luring or Ranging can be accomplished with spells such as "lightning bolt" or "magic missile"
or flamestrike.  To range something in a room, you  cast <flamestrike> <mob> <east>. Also
certain daggers and weapons can be used "throw <dagger> <mob> <east>" to lure mobs. The mob
and any other mob in the same room as it will all charge in and attack you, so it is wise
to make sure there is only one or two mobs in the room you intend to range from.
==See also==
fire, immolure, sorcerer, Lightning Bolt, Magic Missile, cast

