Speak
Speak - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
===================================================
Syntax:  speak <language>
         speak
This command lets you change which language you are currently speaking to a
new one by typing "speak <language>."  Note that you cannot change if you
are not proficient enough in the target language. "Speak" alone shows a
list of your language proficiencies, also your currently spoken language.
	See also:languages

#0

Specialization
Specialization - Last Edited: 2026-10-18
============================================================
At level 30 or higher, a single-class PC without an existing specialization
can choose an allowed path with specialize <name>. Find a matching-class
specialization teacher in the room. A consenting trusted staff character is
also accepted. Any existing respecialization timer must have expired.
Type specialize to list personal choices or specialize list for race/spec
definitions. Not every defined specialization is allowed for every race.
Multiclass characters cannot specialize.
Dragoon paths use Ranger or Mercenary teachers for Dragon Hunter, Shaman or
Druid teachers for Dragon Priest, and Paladin or Anti-Paladin teachers for
Dragon Lancer.
==See also==
Unspecialization, Classes, Multiclass, Speclist

