#0

Spell
Spell - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
===================================================
Spell<br>
A word or formula believed to have magic power.<br>
<br>
In the world of Duris spells are the fundemental tool of all magic-using classes.  While the casting systems, requirements, and spells available vary greatly by race and class, it is on the spell level that magic enters the world of Duris.  Many help files are available detailing spell types, systems, and syntax.  Cast is the best place to start.
See also: cast, Spell System, Spell Slot, Spell Circle, Spell Failure, magic, memorize, pray, assimilate, tupor,commune, caster

#0

Spell circle
Spell circle - Last Edited: 2026-10-18
============================================================
Spells have circle requirements in addition to class/spec eligibility. Circles
1 through 12 open at the following character levels; current progression caps
can limit the levels available.
Level 1 - Circle 1
Level 6 - Circle 2
Level 11 - Circle 3
Level 16 - Circle 4
Level 21 - Circle 5
Level 26 - Circle 6
Level 31 - Circle 7
Level 36 - Circle 8
Level 41 - Circle 9
Level 46 - Circle 10
Level 51 - Circle 11
Level 56 - Circle 12
Being high enough level is not the same as having learned or prepared the
spell. Resource and preparation paths depend on class and race. Secondary-only
multiclass spells cost one extra circle; a spell granted by the primary class
keeps its primary circle.
==See also==
Classes, Memorize, Pray, Commune, Tupor, Multiclass

#0

Spell Failure
Spell Failure - Last Edited: 2007-04-22 22:12:53 by Unknown
===========================================================
A caster who has practiced specific spells for a long period of time
becomes very skilled at casting the spells. He is able to work his magic
without fear of error or incorrectly invoking magic. So, as he gains in
levels, the lower spells become second nature to him. However, when he is
charged with learning new spells of a more complicated nature than he is
used to, he may find it difficult to cast without error. So, casters will
find that they sometimes cannot cast a spell of their highest circle every
time they try. Expect spell failure as you are learning the spells and are
not yet a master of their powers.
==See also==
Spell Circle ,Spell Slot ,Spell System

#0

Spell Slot
Spell Slot - Last Edited: 2007-04-20 14:02:09 by Unknown
========================================================
A caster is able to hold a certain number of spells in each spell circle,
dependent on level. Each spell occupies one spell slot in the given circle.
Casters that commune, assimilate or tupor cannot choose what spells will
fill their specific slots, unlike casters that memorize and pray.
==See also==
Spell Circle ,Spell System

