Thri-Kreen
Thri-Kreen - Last Edited: 2026-08-25 12:00:00 by duris
======================================================
Thri-Kreen, often referred to as "Mantis Warriors", are a unique race of nomadic, insectoid
humanoids native to the arid desert wastes and badlands of Khhiytik. Standing roughly seven
feet tall with sandy-yellow chitinous exoskeletons, large compound eyes, and six limbs (two
powerful legs and four articulate arms), Thri-Kreen are deadly hunters and acrobatic warriors.
They are neutral by nature, choosing their own allegiance in the global race war at birth.

Due to their extraordinary four-armed physiology, Thri-Kreen can wield up to four weapons at
once, including dual two-handed weapons or archery combinations. They can also equip four wrist
items, two sets of sleeves, and two sets of gloves. However, their insectoid anatomy prevents
them from wearing standard body armor, footwear, finger rings, or earrings.

==Strengths==
Thri-Kreen can wield four weapons simultaneously and equip expanded limb gear. They possess
exceptional agility and dexterity, a venomous paralyzing bite, tremendous leaping ability,
and compound vision granting both dayvision and ultravision.

==Weakness==
Thri-Kreen are extremely vulnerable to cold damage, which can shock their circulatory systems
and cause paralysis. They cannot wear standard body armor, boots, or standard jewelry.

