#0
Drider
Drider - Last Edited: 2026-08-25 12:00:00 by duris
==================================================
Driders are terrifying centauric abominations bearing the upper torso and head of a Drow
elf fused at the waist to the eight-legged body of a giant monstrous spider. Revering the dark
spider-goddesses in their subterranean city of Arach-Drathos, driders are an evil race that
combines Drow magical intellect with the lethal predatory traits of arachnids.

Because of their eight-legged spider body, driders possess exceptional balance and stability,
making them nearly impossible to trip or knock down in combat. They can spray thick, sticky webs
to sap their victims' movement before closing in with blade and venomous spellcraft.

==Strengths==
Driders possess innate magic resistance, Web Spray at level 31 to drain movement in combat,
natural groundfighting stability from their spider body, high agility and constitution, and keen
ultravision. They excel as Warriors, Sorcerers, Necromancers, Reavers, and Blighters.

Use 'innate web_spray <target>' to spray a foe (five-minute cooldown). A hit coats the
target for 30 seconds, draining the caster's level divided by 8 in movement each combat
round. Freedom of movement and evade can stop the spray. Moving into another room gives
a 10% chance to tear free, including mounted travel. Another hit refreshes the duration
and replaces the drain; sprays do not stack. The webbing cannot be dispelled.

==Weakness==
Driders suffer from dayblindness under bright sunlight. Due to their spider anatomy, they cannot
wear standard human trousers, greaves, or footwear.

==See also==
