#0
Planetbound Illithid
Planetbound Illithid - Last Edited: 2026-08-25 12:00:00 by duris
================================================================
Planetbound Illithids are a specialized branch of the mind flayer race that has established
permanent subterranean colonies within the deep Underdark city of Ixarkon. While astral illithids
focus on void travel and mental conquest, planetbound illithids have adapted their immense psionic
faculties to terrestrial sorcery, summoning, and elemental manipulation.

Planetbound Illithids retain the terrifying tentacled visage and mental acuity of their kind.
They float effortlessly above the ground using innate levitation and can transition between the
Prime Material and Astral planes at will, commanding powerful summoned allies and devastating
sorceries.

==Strengths==
Planetbound Illithids possess immense Power and Intelligence, very fast spellcasting recovery,
innate magic resistance, innate levitation, planar shifting, and keen ultravision.

==Weakness==
Planetbound Illithids are physically delicate with low Strength and Constitution. They suffer
from dayblindness and sunlight vulnerability on the surface world.

==See also==
* Innate
* Races
* Illithid
* Psionicist
* Sorcerer
* Ixarkon
==Class list==
* Psionicist  :
* Sorcerer    : Wizard, Shadowmage
* Conjurer    : Air Magus, Water Magus, Fire Magus, Earth Magus
* Summoner    : Controller, Mentalist, Naturalist
==Racial Statistics==
Strength    : 83
Agility     : 105
Dexterity   : 105
Constitution: 82
Power       : 125
Intelligence: 120
Wisdom      : 100
Charisma    : 100
Luck        : 100
Karma       : 100
==Racial Traits==
Combat Pulse : average
Spell Pulse  : very good
==Innate abilities==
 levitate (obtained at level 10)
*ultravision
 shift_astral
 shift_prime
*magic resistance
*dayblind
*vulnerable to sun
'*' Designates passive ability.

#0
Wood Elf
Wood Elf - Last Edited: 2026-08-25 12:00:00 by duris
====================================================
Wood Elves, also known as Sylvan or Wild Elves, are reclusive, nature-loving elves who make
their homes in the ancient forests and primeval groves of Duris (hometown Tharnadia). Taller,
more weathered, and sturdier than their delicate Grey Elf kin, wood elves have tanned skin,
earth-toned hair, and keen green or amber eyes that blend seamlessly into the forest canopy.

Wood Elves are legendary for their woodcraft, archery, and wilderness guerrilla tactics. Living
in close communion with nature, they move through dense woodlands with total silence and possess
uncanny vision through thick foliage, making them the premier rangers and druids of the surface
realms.

==Strengths==
Wood Elves possess exceptional wilderness stealth (Outdoor Sneak) and Forest Sight to see through
dense woods. They have innate magic resistance, natural Longsword Mastery, higher Constitution
and Strength than Grey Elves, and keen senses.

==Weakness==
Wood Elves are slightly less focused on pure scholarly arcane magic than Grey Elves, having
slightly lower raw Intelligence.

==See also==
* Innate
* Races
* Grey elf
* Ranger
* Druid
* Tharnadia
==Class list==
No classes available.
==Racial Statistics==
Strength    : 125
Agility     : 115
Dexterity   : 115
Constitution: 135
Power       : 95
Intelligence: 85
Wisdom      : 91
Charisma    : 85
Luck        : 100
Karma       : 100
==Racial Traits==
Combat Pulse : average
Spell Pulse  : above average
==Innate abilities==
*outdoor sneak (obtained at level 11)
*forest sight (obtained at level 11)
*magic resistance
*longsword master (obtained at level 11)
'*' Designates passive ability.

#0
Firbolg
Firbolg - Last Edited: 2026-08-25 12:00:00 by duris
===================================================
Firbolgs are colossal, gentle-hearted giant-kin who dwell in the secluded highland forests,
deep glens, and mountain slopes of Ugta. Standing upwards of nine to ten feet tall with thick,
flowing beards, massive bone structure, and dense musculature, firbolgs are the strongest mortal
creatures on Duris. They live in close harmony with nature and ancient woodland spirits.

Though naturally peaceful and slow to anger, a provoked firbolg is a force of terrifying
destruction. Their immense physical mass allows them to shatter castle gates with Doorbash and
crush armored opponents beneath devastating Bodyslams, making them unmatched frontline titans.

==Strengths==
Firbolgs possess the highest raw Strength (230) in the game and a colossal Constitution (200),
yielding unmatched health and carrying capacity. They possess innate Bodyslam, Doorbash, and
Forest Sight.

==Weakness==
Firbolgs have very slow combat and spell recovery speeds, low agility and dexterity, and an innate
vulnerability to magical damage.

==See also==
* Innate
* Races
* Giant
* Bodyslam
* Ugta
* Shaman
==Class list==
* Warrior     : Swordsman, Guardian
* Shaman      : Elementalist, Spiritualist, Animalist
==Racial Statistics==
Strength    : 230
Agility     : 75
Dexterity   : 75
Constitution: 200
Power       : 65
Intelligence: 75
Wisdom      : 80
Charisma    : 80
Luck        : 90
Karma       : 100
==Racial Traits==
Combat Pulse : atrociously bad
Spell Pulse  : bad
==Innate abilities==
 doorbash
 bodyslam
*forest sight
*magic vulnerability
'*' Designates passive ability.

#0
Tiefling
Tiefling - Last Edited: 2026-08-25 12:00:00 by duris
====================================================
Tieflings are humanoids carrying the planar heritage of fiends, devils, or demons in their
bloodline. Based in the cosmopolitan melting-pot of NaxVaran, tieflings are marked by sharp horns,
prehensile tails, pointed teeth, and eyes of solid color. Despite their infernal ancestry, tieflings
possess free will and choose their own path in the race war, serving on both sides of the conflict.

Tieflings are clever, charismatic, and remarkably adaptable. Their fiendish legacy grants them
natural resistance to both magic and fire, while their acute senses allow them to perceive the
world through both infravision and ultravision. They excel across nearly every class and discipline.

==Strengths==
Tieflings possess innate magic resistance, natural protection from fire, and dual infravision and
ultravision. They have high Intelligence, Charisma, Agility, and Dexterity, alongside vast class
versatility.

==Weakness==
Tieflings face widespread social prejudice from conservative cultures, and possess average
physical constitution.

==See also==
* Innate
* Races
* Infravision
* Ultravision
* NaxVaran
* Paladin
* Anti-Paladin
==Class list==
* Warrior     : Swordsman, Guardian, Swashbuckler
* Ranger      : Blademaster, Huntsman, Marshall
* Paladin     : Crusader, Cavalier
* Anti-Paladin: Dark Knight, Demonic Rider, Violator
* Cleric      : Zealot, Healer, Holyman
* Monk        : Red Dragon, Elaphidist
* Shaman      : Elementalist, Spiritualist, Animalist
* Sorcerer    : Wildmage, Wizard, Shadowmage
* Conjurer    : Air Magus, Water Magus, Fire Magus, Earth Magus
* Rogue       : Assassin, Thief
* Mercenary   : Brigand, Bounty Hunter
* Bard        : Disharmonist, Scoundrel, Minstrel
* Reaver      : Ice Reaver, Flame Reaver, Shock Reaver, Earth Reaver
* Illusionist : Magician, Dark Dreamer
* Ethermancer : Tempest Magus, Frost Magus, Star Magus
* Summoner    : Controller, Mentalist, Naturalist
* Dragoon     : Dragon Hunter, Dragon Priest, Dragon Lancer
==Racial Statistics==
Strength    : 100
