#0

Divineboon
Divineboon - Last Edited: 2026-10-23 00:30:00 by Duris
===========================================================================
Staff command: divineboon status | pause | resume | replace <slot> | force |
               history

Status shows committed memory state, pending writes, stable boon IDs, both
side targets, next UTC opportunity and validated candidate counts. History
shows the last sixteen retired boons, including replaced and expired events;
older snapshots begin this staff history empty.

Pause prevents new spawns without freezing expiry. Resume consumes the current
hour and permits the next normal opportunity. Replace expires one active
numbered slot, recording its identity; refill waits for the next normal hour.
Force retries only a due, unconsumed hourly opportunity. It cannot bypass
pause, timing, target safety, event limits or account caps, or reroll a prepared
choice after queue refusal. Commands use the same durable state writer as
normal rotation. A submitted update is effective only after commit; status
reports pending confirmation. Repeated identical requests cannot duplicate
an opportunity. Mutations and force requests are recorded in the staff log.

Boot closes new legacy work, finishes known accepted live callbacks and retains
old receipts without recipient checkpoint proof for staff reconciliation.
Flat receipts stay pending; SQL outbox records stay in its existing dead-letter
queue (world persistence reports them). An old receipt alone cannot tell whether
a crash occurred just before or just after payment. Never replay or acknowledge
these ambiguous records blindly. Inspect the original receipt, recipient save
and matching reward ledger before reconciling it. No balances are converted or
deleted. Divine activation starts with an empty state before normal rotation.
Do not change back to old code while accepted rewards are unresolved.
See also: BOON, DIVINE BOONS

